 ## What this adds
 
 * The diagnostic-only wrapper allocates unique, non-reusable slots before serializing simultaneous joins. It keeps normal room, input, guest identity, economy session, traffic, snapshot and timer code, and stages the existing seed-0 Roadsters at the recorded corridors. A random bearer secret is required for every room socket and staging/status/export operation. Runtime routing checks the separate diagnostic Preview hostname and marker; only disposable `gha-<run>-<attempt>` rooms are accepted. The sample config is explicitly for `wrangler dev --local` and its repeated `a` token is not a live secret.
-* Four independently runnable groups each use 16 real `Session` instances and header-bearing Node WebSockets. They wait until all 64 unique slots have joined and guest identities and economy sessions are ready. Begin fences controls and starts the existing scheduler. Each Session must observe fresh advancing ticks before a shared warmup/start tick. It uses a speed-bounded straight control and stores bounded raw input and snapshot observations; overflow is incomplete. Four groups signal completion before the first group exports bounded tick-level pose/indicator pages.
-* Contact records are deliberately **incomplete**: `recordTick()` samples after each whole tick and may miss a substep collision, brief overlap or barrier. `ContactTrace` always uses `authoritativeCoverage=false` in this worker, and the driver always reports `authoritative-substep-contact-coverage-unavailable`. It detects bad or missing sample sequences, unexpected support/lane, sampled damage/impulse, unsealed trace and bounded pose/event overflow; none of that proves an unobstructed interval. The required true authoritative per-substep event hooks do not exist here.
+* Four independently runnable groups each use 16 real `Session` instances and header-bearing Node WebSockets. They wait until all 64 unique slots have joined and guest identities and economy sessions are ready. Begin fences controls and starts the existing scheduler. Each Session must observe fresh advancing ticks before a shared warmup/start tick. It uses a speed-bounded straight control and stores bounded raw input and snapshot observations; overflow is incomplete. Four groups signal completion before the first group exports bounded substep pose/event pages.
+* Diagnostic-only hooks surround every authoritative `advance` substep and record real entity-contact, ground static-solid, progression, island-jump-wall and stunt-ramp-wall decisions, plus end-of-substep poses with tick, index and substep count. The hooks flag ferry-secured or out-of-corridor/special-surface states, identity/revision changes, gaps and overflow. Events may capture contacts that a tick snapshot would miss. This is still **incomplete**: for example ferry/deck blocking inside `followSupport`, dome constraints, some landing and post-separation special-wall handling, and any transient unsupported path require further audit. Begin/end state checks alone cannot rule those out. `ContactTrace` keeps `authoritativeCoverage=false`, and every driver reports `authoritative-substep-contact-coverage-unavailable`; no absence-of-contact claim follows from these records. An instrumentation exception marks the trace invalid, not complete.
 * The 64 candidate lanes came from the local `d05d6f4` preflight. The committed `shared/` tree is unchanged between that revision and `a53d0998`, but the v2 diagnostic modifies `shared/tick-input.ts` and this does not verify a later release. Rerun static and spawn-fit checks against the final source; sampled surface checks do not prove uninterrupted support or dynamic traffic avoidance. Guest economy hooks are present; saved-driver writes, recovery and financial operations are not exercised by the workload.
 
